//! `inventory.rs` — **THE PRODUCER'S SURFACE, AS THIS CONSUMER'S BUILD INPUT.**
//!
//! **GENERATED BY `tools/make-inventory.py`, BESIDE `inventory.json`, IN ONE RUN.**
//! Hand-editing it is the one thing the seam cannot survive: it is the producer's
//! surface as the PRODUCER stated it, and a consumer that edited it would be
//! compiling against its own opinion. `tools/seamdiff --inventory` asserts this
//! file and `inventory.json` are the same surface at the same commit, and names
//! the field that moved when they are not.
//!
//! Read from `cauldron` at **`3c6de48`**
//! (3c6de48d4da0951c662ddd37badcfd2db4c174a2), via `declared:cargo run -p threads --bin shapes-manifest`.
//!
//! ## What is here, and what a missing name looks like
//!
//! * [`methods`] — one [`Method`] const per method the producer dispatches.
//! * one module per shape — one [`Carried`] const per cell it declares, plus the
//!   field names and closed vocabularies of each cell, one level deep.
//!
//! A name that is not here is a name the producer does not serve, and the
//! failure is rustc's own — `error[E0425]: cannot find value ... in module ...`
//! — in the consumer's build, at the line that depends on it. The list of what
//! there IS is this file, and the slices `METHODS`, `CELLS` and `SHARED` carry
//! the same lists for a reader that wants them at runtime.
//!
//! **TIME SKEW IS NOT COVERED AND CANNOT BE.** This is the surface at the commit
//! above; the producer may have moved since. `vendor-chassis.sh` refuses a bump
//! whose producer surface moved, and rule 2.6 refuses a stale CONTRACT at link.
//! Nothing in a consumer's build can see the producer's current surface.

// Most of this module is vocabulary a given face does not use. A surface is not
// dead code for being larger than one consumer's appetite.
#![allow(dead_code)]

